    "result": "## Summary\n\nI have successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's what was completed:\n\n### **Feature Implementation**\n\n\u2705 **CLI Option** (`frai eval --threshold <metric>=<min>`)\n- Can be specified multiple times\n- Validates format: must be `<metric>=<number>`\n- Validates range: number must be 0-1\n- Exit code 0 if all pass, 1 if any fail, 2 for usage errors\n\n\u2705 **Core Logic** (frai-core/eval)\n- `generateReport()` accepts optional `thresholds` object\n- Computes pass/fail for each threshold\n- Metric with no score fails the threshold\n- Report includes `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array only when thresholds provided\n\n\u2705 **Report Formats**\n- **JSON**: Adds `passed` and `thresholds` fields\n- **Markdown**: Adds \"## Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL status\n\n\u2705 **Error Handling**\n- Malformed thresholds: exit 2 with error message\n- Unknown metrics: exit 2 listing valid metrics\n- Out-of-range values: exit 2 with explanation\n\n### **Testing**\n\u2705 5 new threshold tests in frai-core (all passing)\n\u2705 Built packages successfully\n\u2705 End-to-end CLI testing verified:\n  - Passing thresholds \u2192 exit 0\n  - Failing thresholds \u2192 exit 1\n  - Invalid thresholds \u2192 exit 2\n  - Multiple thresholds supported\n  - Markdown and JSON formats both work\n\n### **Files Changed**\n1. `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js` - Added threshold logic to generateReport\n2. `packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js` - Added Thresholds section to markdown\n3. `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` - Added CLI option, parsing, validation, and exit code handling\n4. `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js` - Added 5 comprehensive threshold tests\n\n### **Compatibility**\n- Without `--threshold`: behavior unchanged (exit 0, no threshold data in report)\n- SDK users can pass `thresholds` object to `generateReport()`\n- Works with custom metrics via SDK\n\nAll requirements from the feature request have been implemented and verified working correctly.",
